# Frame list for "Neanderthals vs Us". One frame per script timestamp.
# The recorded script restarts at 0:00 twice, so it's split into Part 1, Part 2 and Part 3.
STYLE = ("Medium-skill MS Paint doodle: crude, rushed, hand-made, funny and deliberately clumsy, beginner level. Simple cartoon "
         "stick-style characters with round heads, simple bodies, dot or circle eyes and clear simple facial expressions. Thick "
         "uneven wobbly black outlines, hand-drawn lines, flat colour fills only (green, brown, grey, red, yellow, orange, blue). "
         "Fill the whole frame: flat-coloured sky or wall and ground plus a few simple doodled background details made of basic "
         "shapes. Red arrows or red question marks for emphasis. NO shading, gradients, 3D or cinematic lighting; not polished, "
         "not Disney or anime, not vector art, no complex textures, no realistic people, not gory. Uncluttered, subject centred, "
         "nothing cropped, no broken anatomy. Wide horizontal 16:9 YouTube still. Any text: short handwritten scrawl, correctly "
         "spelled and legible. SCENE: ")

